# Kotlin

- The JDK comes only from the `java` tool (mise, Temurin LTS). Do not use
  `jvmToolchain`, `java { toolchain }` or the foojay resolver.
- Set the bytecode target with `jvmTarget`, `-Xjdk-release` and
  `options.release`.
- Run Gradle only as `./gradlew`. Do not use `kotlinc` or a system `gradle`.
- The Kotlin compiler version is the version of the Kotlin Gradle plugin in
  the version catalog.
- Set `allWarningsAsErrors = true`.
- Do not use `!!`. Give a platform type an explicit type at its first use.
- Each API has one failure shape: an own exception hierarchy or a sealed
  result. Use `require` and `check` only for a programmer error.
- Write the tests with `kotlin.test` on JUnit 5, and `runTest` for coroutine
  code. Kover measures the coverage. Use hand-written fakes, not mocks.
- The language server is `mise x -- kotlin-lsp --stdio` (the dev environment,
  on macOS).

## In a library

- Turn on the explicit API mode (`explicitApi()`).
- Depend only on the API artifacts of SLF4J, Micrometer and OpenTelemetry.
- Read no environment variable and no system property. The caller gives the
  configuration as a value.

Read `references/conventions.md` for the conventions, and
`references/local.md` for the own rules of this repository.
